        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Welcome to the Aisphere documentation website! Aisphere is an AI-native service infrastructure platform built around a specification-driven microservice framework.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="what-is-aisphere">What is Aisphere?<a href="https://aisphereio.github.io/en/blog/welcome#what-is-aisphere" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What is Aisphere?" title="Direct link to What is Aisphere?" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Aisphere consists of several key components:</p>
<ul>
<li class=""><strong>Kernel</strong> — The specification-driven microservice foundation framework</li>
<li class=""><strong>IAM</strong> — Identity and access management service</li>
<li class=""><strong>Hub</strong> — AIHub business service for skill management</li>
<li class=""><strong>Gateway</strong> — Edge gateway for routing and access control</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="whats-next">What's Next?<a href="https://aisphereio.github.io/en/blog/welcome#whats-next" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What's Next?" title="Direct link to What's Next?" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<ul>
<li class="">Explore the <a class="" href="https://aisphereio.github.io/en/docs/kernel/intro">Kernel documentation</a> to get started</li>
<li class="">Check out the <a class="" href="https://aisphereio.github.io/en/docs/guides/architecture">architecture overview</a></li>
<li class="">Follow the <a class="" href="https://aisphereio.github.io/en/docs/guides/quickstart">quick start guide</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Stay tuned for more updates!</p>]]></content>
